        "id": 105392,
        "name": "Ronway",
        "username": "Ronway",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/{size}/1856_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-06-01T13:52:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I don't think it is game breaking if you decide to make a scrap pile&nbsp;for&nbsp;both Opposition decks. The only reason they go to the bottom is to reduce the amount of shuffling in the game. Doing so will cause all four decks to go into a scrap pile. Then whenever a deck runs out, you do the reshuffling the corresponding trash and make the new deck. Strike Force will never run out of cards, since the all the starting decks consist of 4 boost, unless there is a way to scrap boost that I don't remember.</p>",
